// REJECTED — a provide-method PARAMETER takes the name of a module `fn` that
// the same body CALLS, so `tag("x")` has two readings and the tiers do not pick
// the same one: a python, TypeScript, Rust or Go local shadows the function,
// while a Java local does not shadow a static method of that name. Rename the
// parameter.
//
// The `let` form of the same shadowing is refused with this message (issue
// #445, `shadowed_module_fn_call.rvl`), and a local named like a constructor
// shadows it (#2490). The parameter form used to be the one case that
// slipped past the check and dropped the binding silently: both compilers
// lowered `tag("x")` to a call of the module `fn tag` (issue #2544).
//
// expected error:
//   `tag` is bound here and called in this body

fn tag(s: Str) -> Str { return s }

service Cache {
  fn f(tag: Str) -> Str
}

component C provides cache: Cache {
  provide cache {
    fn f(tag) = tag("x")
  }
}
